      "id": 494985,
      "username": "tcbinfotech",
      "name": "TCB Infotech",
      "created_at": "2026-02-25T03:32:27.700Z",
      "cooked": "<p>For role-based workspace layouts in Frappe, the simplest approach is:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Create a separate Public Workspace for each role e.g. “Sales Rep Desk”.</li>\n<li>In each workspace’s settings, assign the Roles that should see it users without those roles won’t see it.</li>\n<li>Set the Home Page field on the Role doctype to point to that workspace, so users land there after login.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>If you need more granular control (whitelist/blacklist per workspace), check out the community app workspaceperms:</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox githubrepo\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/pstuhlmueller/workspaceperms\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/pstuhlmueller/workspaceperms\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">github.com</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <div class=\"github-row\" data-github-private-repo=\"false\">\n  <img width=\"690\" height=\"344\" src=\"https://opengraph.githubassets.com/9077d2664eccb634b9a810f047f52459/pstuhlmueller/workspaceperms\" class=\"thumbnail\">\n\n  <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/pstuhlmueller/workspaceperms\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">GitHub - pstuhlmueller/workspaceperms: Manage the availability of workspaces within...</a></h3>\n\n    <p><span class=\"github-repo-description\">Manage the availability of workspaces within Frappe/ ERPNext (sidebar) based on user-roles</span></p>\n</div>\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n\n<p>This covers most use cases without any custom development.</p>",
